        model_answer="Both boxes move together, so treat them as one 6 kg object: a = F ÷ m = 12 ÷ 6 = 2 m/s². The only horizontal force on the 4 kg box is the push from the 2 kg box, so F = ma = 4 × 2 = 8 N. By Newton's third law the 4 kg box pushes back on the 2 kg box with 8 N, so the resultant on the 2 kg box is 12 − 8 = 4 N, which gives 4 ÷ 2 = 2 m/s², consistent.",
